From 12a957e93a567596dde8e7a4980d5c26c41bad90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:19:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep collecting the blob while it grows; age out stale
 manifests

Two device findings from 2026-11-17 turned two assumptions over.

1. The blob is not finished when it first becomes readable, and reading does not consume it.
   Measured on the same night:
     08:58 read -> 112,632 bytes, beats up to 08:11
     14:08 read -> 119,548 bytes, beats up to 08:46
   The watch kept appending for another 35 minutes after the first readable copy appeared,
   and the earlier read did not destroy anything. So the morning retry no longer stops on the
   first success: it keeps asking hourly until 13:00, and every distinct version is archived
   (identical bytes are deduplicated by sha256, so a repeated read costs nothing).

2. Manifests relocated for a schema bump were never pruned. They are renamed to
   manifest-<stamp>.json.v<n>.stale, which no longer matches the batch pattern, so they
   accumulated for ever. pruneBatches() now also recognises that suffix and ages them out on
   the same KEEP_BATCH_DAYS rule.

Device-verified this session:
  - schema relocation: with export_schema.txt forced to 5, an export renamed all 10 existing
    manifests to .v5.stale, left exactly one manifest-<stamp>.json, and wrote 6 to the marker
  - retention: a planted 20-day-old manifest + CSV pair was deleted by the next export, and
    the recent batches were untouched (231 CSVs before/after accounting for the new batch)
  - sleep_state archival: 144 bytes saved twice, as sleep_state_<epoch_ms>.bin
  - periodic sync back to 6 h: next fire 20:00

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK, installed.
---
 .../gadgetbridge/database/DatabaseExportWorker.kt        | 5 +++++
 .../service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java    | 9 +++++++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/database/DatabaseExportWorker.kt b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/database/DatabaseExportWorker.kt
index 8a11f71..2cdaeaf 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/database/DatabaseExportWorker.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/database/DatabaseExportWorker.kt
@@ -1106,9 +1106,14 @@ class DatabaseExportWorker(
             val parser = SimpleDateFormat("yyyyMMdd-HHmmss", Locale.US)
             val kinds = DELTA_TABLES.joinToString("|") { Regex.escape(it.kind) }
             val batchFile = Regex("^(?:manifest|$kinds)-(\\d{8}-\\d{6})\\.(?:json|csv)$")
+            // Manifests of an older schema are renamed to `manifest-<stamp>.json.v<n>.stale` so a
+            // consumer's `manifest-*.json` glob skips them. They still carry a stamp, so they age
+            // out on the same rule instead of accumulating for ever.
+            val staleManifest = Regex("^manifest-(\\d{8}-\\d{6})\\.json\\.v\\d+\\.stale$")
             for ((name, doc) in listDocuments(location)) {
                 val staleTmp = name.endsWith(".json.tmp") && name != "manifest-$currentBatch.json.tmp"
                 val stampText = batchFile.matchEntire(name)?.groupValues?.get(1)
+                    ?: staleManifest.matchEntire(name)?.groupValues?.get(1)
                 val expired = if (stampText == null || stampText == currentBatch) {
                     false
                 } else {
diff --git a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
index 3274e72..6abc1be 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
@@ -759,8 +759,11 @@ public class HuaweiSupportProvider {
                                     return;
                                 }
                                 LOG.info("FULLDUMP sleep_data bytes={}", data.length);
-                                sleepRetryCount = 0;
-                                sleepRetryHandler.removeCallbacks(sleepRetry);
+                                // Do NOT stop here. Measured 2026-11-17: the first readable copy
+                                // (08:58, 112,632 B) covered beats up to 08:11, while a later read
+                                // (14:08, 119,548 B) covered up to 08:46 — the watch kept appending.
+                                // So the morning retries continue, and each distinct version is
+                                // archived (identical ones are deduplicated by sha256).
                                 try {
                                     java.io.File dir = new java.io.File(
                                             getContext().getExternalFilesDir(null), "dump");
@@ -769,11 +772,13 @@ public class HuaweiSupportProvider {
                                 } catch (Exception e) {
                                     LOG.error("FULLDUMP save failed", e);
                                 }
+                                scheduleMorningRetry();
                             }
 
                             @Override
                             public void downloadException(HuaweiFileDownloadManager.HuaweiFileDownloadException e) {
                                 LOG.info("FULLDUMP sleep_data failed: {}", e.getMessage());
+                                scheduleMorningRetry();
                             }
                         }), false);
         LOG.info("FULLDUMP requested {} -> {}", start, end);
